Design for Maintenance or Maintainability is one of the main circular strategy (X1) and refers to the ability of the system to be maintained or restored to serviceable operation. Easy, cost, location and time of maintenance have an important impact on the execution of the strategy. The strategy can be applied to product, components or materials. In designing for Maintenance the primary task for designers is to determinate how to replace the revenue from the selling of the product with the revenue from services related to the maintenance of the product.